  "replication": {
    "note": "Second independent run of the identical configuration, same frozen binary, recorded 2026-09-08 15:31-15:58 as the control arm of an allocator comparison.",
    "agreement": [
      "Live heap agrees to within 0.1-0.8 percent at every phase. Bytes per view at the traversal peak are 653/637/656 against 653/637/657 in the first run: the load-bearing quantity reproduces to within 0.2 percent.",
      "Retained RSS does not reproduce nearly as tightly: rounds two and three differ by 5.9 percent, and G3 comes out 477.3/483.5/513.4 MiB against 476.4/514.8/546.7 MiB.",
      "All of the variation is therefore in the allocator-retained component, which depends on thread scheduling and allocation interleaving, and none of it is in the live data. This is what makes the live-peak conclusion safe to build weeks of work on and the retained-RSS numbers unsafe to quote to three significant figures.",
      "G3 fails in both runs in every round, by 1.86x to 2.14x."
    ],
